                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17074104" author="nizhikov" created="Thu, 2 Apr 2020 21:43:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I found that .net service proxy doesn&apos;t work if method param is&lt;br/&gt;
 java.sql.Timestamp &amp;lt;-&amp;gt; DateTime or &lt;br/&gt;
java.util.UUID &amp;lt;-&amp;gt; Guid.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The PR fixes it - &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/7618&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/7618&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can you take a look at my changes?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17074542" author="ptupitsyn" created="Fri, 3 Apr 2020 12:25:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=nizhikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;nizhikov&quot;&gt;nizhikov&lt;/a&gt; looks like existing behavior is broken - check BinaryDataTimeTest, and many other tests fail with `DateTime is not UTC. Only UTC DateTime can be used for interop with other platforms.` exception. We can&apos;t break user code this way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related ticket: &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12824&quot; title=&quot;.NET: Interoperable DateTime&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-12824&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-12824&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17074543" author="nizhikov" created="Fri, 3 Apr 2020 12:27:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the answer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, I saw it and I will fix these tests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do we have to support DateTime as a service parameter?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17074551" author="ptupitsyn" created="Fri, 3 Apr 2020 12:57:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=nizhikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;nizhikov&quot;&gt;nizhikov&lt;/a&gt; yes, I think we should. I looked into the code, and the fix seems to be simple. Update `ServiceProxySerializer.GetPlatformArgWriter` method with the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (arg is DateTime)
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; (writer, o) =&amp;gt; writer.WriteTimestamp((DateTime) arg);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Java service calls require special treatment of arguments. We do that for other types in GetPlatformArgWriter already.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It makes sense to pass .NET -&amp;gt; .NET service args as DateTime object (works already), but for Java service we can only use `WriteTimestamp`, which requires UTC value, and will throw otherwise. And this only affects Services,  normal binary object handling remains as is.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17075079" author="nizhikov" created="Sat, 4 Apr 2020 08:16:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I applier your suggestions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like now there is no new test fails - &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5188422&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAllNet&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5188422&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAllNet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can you, please, take a look one more time.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17075279" author="ptupitsyn" created="Sat, 4 Apr 2020 20:12:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=nizhikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;nizhikov&quot;&gt;nizhikov&lt;/a&gt; looks good to me, thank you!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17075282" author="nizhikov" created="Sat, 4 Apr 2020 20:18:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;&#160;Thanks for the review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
